WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.990
TritonAI Harness is UC San Diego's AI workspace on your desktop.

2
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:09.030
You hand it real work, and it delivers finished results,

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.480
using your files and campus systems.

4
00:00:12.844 --> 00:00:14.024
Here it is, with a made-up project:

5
00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:16.324
Jordan's fall workshop pilot.

6
00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:18.994
Qualtrics already reports the survey,

7
00:00:19.224 --> 00:00:21.674
but Jordan wants the team's own questions answered,

8
00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:23.554
so I hand it the raw results.

9
00:00:25.002 --> 00:00:26.312
About half a minute later:

10
00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:29.012
averages for every question, the top comments,

11
00:00:29.222 --> 00:00:30.692
and the missing data flagged,

12
00:00:30.942 --> 00:00:33.472
saved as a file that opens right beside the thread.

13
00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:37.447
Jordan has ten minutes with leaders next week,

14
00:00:37.657 --> 00:00:40.557
so the meeting notes and the survey become a briefing deck

15
00:00:40.577 --> 00:00:42.727
on the official UC San Diego template.

16
00:00:44.114 --> 00:00:46.624
Eight slides, with charts and speaker notes,

17
00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.404
all built from the source files.

18
00:00:49.054 --> 00:00:50.564
You can page through it right in the Harness.

19
00:00:52.005 --> 00:00:54.295
It plugs into the campus systems you already use:

20
00:00:54.945 --> 00:01:02.335
GitHub, Google Workspace, Jira, Kuali Build, Lucid, Microsoft 365, and n8n,

21
00:01:02.565 --> 00:01:05.775
plus UCSD Assistant for public campus sources.

22
00:01:07.246 --> 00:01:09.636
Here it reads an n8n workflow,

23
00:01:10.206 --> 00:01:12.236
explains each step in plain language,

24
00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.416
and points out that the workflow is turned off.

25
00:01:16.678 --> 00:01:18.888
With GitHub, it reviews a code change:

26
00:01:19.598 --> 00:01:23.248
what changed, which files, and whether the build passed.

27
00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:25.899
And it builds software.

28
00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:29.399
A Microsoft Form would cover a basic sign-up,

29
00:01:29.429 --> 00:01:31.799
but Jordan's team wants the campus look,

30
00:01:32.089 --> 00:01:34.369
and every sign-up in its own n8n workflow.

31
00:01:34.389 --> 00:01:38.599
Here's that app, on the official campus design system.

32
00:01:39.919 --> 00:01:40.629
Coming soon:

33
00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:42.059
self-service hosting,

34
00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:45.999
so the apps you build in the Harness can go live

35
00:01:46.019 --> 00:01:46.689
for campus.

36
00:01:48.142 --> 00:01:50.632
When a campus tool does the job, use it.

37
00:01:51.442 --> 00:01:54.252
When you need it your way, build it with the Harness.

38
00:01:55.753 --> 00:01:56.653
That's TritonAI Harness:

39
00:01:56.673 --> 00:02:01.943
real work, finished on your desktop, with campus tools built in.
